  "coverage": [
    "Exact rand_chacha/Goldilocks sequences for seeds, stream IDs, odd word offsets, 64-bit counters, stream-end and multi-batch boundaries.",
    "Stable dense-rejection compaction across lane/tile boundaries and a full 1,048,576-candidate batch; guards preserve unwritten output and aliased scratch is rejected before submission.",
    "Shared byte planners retain the existing OpenCL implementation. Aggregate bytes, allocation counts, geometry, output limits and stream-state limits reject before consumption.",
    "Clones share the cursor; construction snapshots share the immutable private key while copying the position. Failed sampling, exhaustion and unwinds retire all related handles.",
    "The proof RNG adapter prohibits CPU use after CUDA activation. A failed proof group also retires escaped device aliases; a failed import leaves its source retired.",
    "Normal host RNG destruction is followed by a volatile wipe of its owned MaybeUninit storage, including cached blocks and padding. Seed staging copies are wiped; native private buffers retain the existing synchronous cleanup.",
    "Fresh random base-field salt matrices feed native salted commitments. CPU Merkle oracles match, with no sample upload or readback before the audit; aliases retain allocation ownership.",
    "NVRTC compilation succeeds for compute_70 and compute_120. Native and adapter suites pass memcheck, racecheck and synccheck. The intentional missing-kernel API error runs outside sanitizer coverage.",
    "OpenCL sampler/planner/proof-RNG, challenger, scalar, quotient and streaming allocation regressions pass; CPU/OpenCL library, Apple Metal cross-compilation and standalone CUDA builds pass."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This checkpoint does not produce complete native CUDA wallet or recursive proofs. Hiding PCS, salt replay, witness/preprocessing/lookup evaluation, openings/FRI/final polynomials and backend/stage/worker integration remain unfinished.",
    "The existing default backend, proof profile, verification rules and production admission policy are unchanged.",
    "V100 CUDA execution and Apple Metal execution remain untested on this host.",
    "The manual sampler benchmark is compiled but excluded from correctness qualification. No complete-proof or transaction throughput is established here."
  ],
  "controller_note": "The first controller stopped after a passing racecheck because it expected memcheck summary syntax. The corrected controller retained and checked that passing log, verified unchanged source/binaries, and ran the remaining checks. Both controller logs are preserved. The subsequent streaming-only compiler job exceeded the 3 GiB host cap after all GPU checks passed; it was retried with one build job, a 6 GiB host cap and zero swap. The failed build log is retained.",
